a Palace. But for our match in Paris coinciding with the inter-county championship, Carter,Penny,Footer and Cohen would have been included in the Surrey team. Belgravians are (l to r) rear row: W.L. Bayliss (President), A.R. Shaw. Centre row: C.T. Carter, A.W. Penny, J.A. Kemp, L.J. Cohen. Front row: A.E. Taylor, H.E. Footer. The central figure is, of course, J.C. Crump and the man on the extreme right, Denis Brickwood--then of Mitcham AC. Six days after these teams were televised by the Baird process, it was announced by the B.B.C. that the E.M.I. process would be adopted!","id":"B158-24","w":"March 1966"},{"f":"crops/B161/B161-p37-world-sports-cuttings.jpg","c":"Press cuttings from \"World Sports\" by Neil Allen","id":"B161-58","w":"March 1967"}],"photo":{"file":"crops/B158/B158-p11-surrey-intercounty-team-1937.jpg","caption":"27th January 1937---Part of Belgrave's winning team which beat U.S.M. (Paris) pose with Surrey's winning inter-county team at the Television studios, Alexandra Palace. But for our match in Paris coinciding with the inter-county championship, Carter,Penny,Footer and Cohen would have been included in the Surrey team. Belgravians are (l to r) rear row: W.L. Bayliss (President), A.R. Shaw. Centre row: C.T. Carter, A.W. Penny, J.A. Kemp, L.J. Cohen. Front row: A.E. Taylor, H.E. Footer. The central figure is, of course, J.C. Crump and the man on the extreme right, Denis Brickwood--then of Mitcham AC. Six days after these teams were televised by the Baird process, it was announced by the B.B.C. that the E.M.I. process would be adopted!","source":"B158-24","when":"March 1966"},"x":1,"share":{"d":"Les Cohen in The Belgravian, the Belgrave Harriers club gazette, 1962–2001: 28 mentions in 24 issues, 13 race results and 2 photographs.","img":"https://belgravian-images.stephendgardner.workers.dev/belgravian/crops/B158/B158-p11-surrey-intercounty-team-1937.jpg","u":"https://stephengardner1.github.io/belgrave-harriers-data/belgravian/read/share/p-les-cohen.html"},"legend":false}